<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Teljoy year share back in profit.</title>
<headline>Teljoy year share back in profit.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre exceptional items     9.5     vs    58.7 loss</p>
<p>    - after exceptional items  21.0     vs    62.4 loss</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			none     vs    none</p>
<p>    Attrib income		  17.5     vs    48.2 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  25.9     vs    78.3 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			  0.28 refund  vs     2.0</p>
<p>    Turnover			606.2     vs   567.2</p>
<p>Full name: Teljoy Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company made an exceptional profit of 16.2 million rand on the sale of 10 percent of Teljoy Cellular division.</p>
<p>Chief executive Johann Pieterse said in a statement that both cellular and television divisions were expected to trade profitably and the group earnings before exceptional items would increase &quot;substantially&quot; in the new financial year.</p>
<p>&quot;The health of the group has improved dramatically but it is too early to claim victory,&quot; he said, attributing the turnaround to &quot;good basic housekeeping -- improving systems and administration, getting on top of the fraud problem, reducing bad debts and 'churn'&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
